  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table><thead><tr><th><div>Serum Zinc Level</div></th><th><div>Interpretation</div></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><div>Normal</div></td><td><div>Indicates sufficient zinc in the blood and adequate zinc status for normal bodily functions.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Low</div></td><td><div>May suggest zinc deficiency due to inadequate dietary intake, malabsorption, chronic illnesses, certain medications, or other factors. Symptoms of zinc deficiency may include delayed wound healing, hair loss, loss of appetite, impaired immune function, and skin rashes. Further evaluation is necessary for confirmation and appropriate management.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>High</div></td><td><div>Less common, may be associated with excessive zinc intake from supplements or certain medical conditions. Additional assessment is needed to determine the cause and whether any intervention is required.</div></td></tr></tbody></table>",
